\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Buying power. If you are in a position to buy power: take it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The players who buy power most efficiently, win.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 More broadly: buying health - what is the impact this decision will have on my health bar -- now, and later.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 So, the decision to level:}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 you can buy power for 'x' amount of gold. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 how much gold is this sacrificing for how much health?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 ---need to specify this.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 SO thats how you evaluate each decision}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 when you make efficient tradeoffs of gold for power/health, it was a good decision.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Be strong now, or weaker later, vs be weaker now, vs stronger later.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Augments:}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Economy, Item, Combat}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Items are strongest now, then combat, then economy.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 When to take strongest now aguments, vs. strongest in the future?}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 --when you have upgraded units. Then it is very efficient.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 --you take econ when you have no board, because taking items won't make you much stronger.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 So, on 2-1}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 90th percentile - 3 upgraded 1 cost units + 2 trait + Max item Slam}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \tab --most comfortable picking item aug, and leveling to win.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 From here, the weaker your comp is, the worse it is to do this. And it gets worse to do this very quickly.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 75th percentile - 2 upgraded 1 costs + 2 traits + good slam}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 50th percentile - 1 upgraded 1 cost + 2 traits + weak slam}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \tab --the game heavily rewards streaking - absolute strongest or weakest. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 **When you click an augment, you want to have an idea of what you want to do on the stage. Either play slow and not level--build up gold through interest. Or plays strong - lose gold and save health.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 25th percentile - 1 upgrade OR 1 slam + 1 or 2 traits}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 If you try to play strong with anything less than a 75th percentile board, you're very likely to win less than 4/5 rounds.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 If you do that, that is not a spot you want to invest to be in. You would prefer to take 1 or two more losses in exchange for making the gold by not leveling, and playing for a stronger board.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 5 streak = at least 12 gold}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Losing 1 round = 30% less gold = ~9 gold.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 If you play the stage slow, you are expected to gain about 3-4 gold.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 (not leveling early, making more interest).}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 So, winning 4/5 rounds is kind've okay. But losing any more than that, and you're making less gold than you otherwise would have.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 ****IF you are behind, you want the game to put resources into your hand first, before you lean in to invest to make your game stronger***}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 3-2 augment}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The game has a natural oscilliation in power through the lobby. Because the game is constantly giving low health players more power on average, from carousel choice, to items in neutrals, etc. So if you are at the top, and unlucky, you are slipping in power. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 SO, even if you are streaking, you do not pick an augment to maintain a streak. You pick for what you expect to be able to do in the stage. Rerollers may start hitting, and youre potential power gain is weak, then its not great to go for items.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 So, pairs, potential components - you are more likely to win coming rounds if you have 4 pairs compared to zero.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 if you have no pairs on your bench, you are guaranteed to lose the next three rounds to anyone who is trying to win.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 So a decision to sell bench units can is, essentially, a decision to say, in 3 rounds, i'm going to lose.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 YOu don't want 9 or 10 loss playing level 8, so losing early is brutal.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It's fine for reroll, because you spike earlier.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 if you are playing 2 cost reroll - on 3-2, you need to level to 6 and roll for 2 star tank and carry.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 for 3 cost reroll, if you are lose-streaking early, you have to level at 3-5. If you are winning early, level at 4-1.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 for 8 cost reroll, low health is 4-2, high health you should be willing to delay rolldown to 4-5.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 rolling early when contested is a fallacy.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 You need more total gold when contested to reach your board.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Instead of rolling early, the advantage gained is to play a wider variety of units, and knowing what can fit into your comp.}
